The conversation focused on formatting a reference list for a proposal. James provided an extensive reference list and requested a concise format similar to that used in *Nature*. I generated a numbered list using full titles and journal names. James then asked for the use of "et al." for citations with more than two authors and to place the year after the authors. Following this, he inquired about further condensing the list for a less formal proposal, ultimately deciding to drop titles to retain essential information while minimizing space.
